			<div class="content" id="post-content-3883113">
									

<p>Very glad you enjoyed this, Wils. :)</p>
<p>Thanks also for the suggestions, they're both good points which I'll add to my list of things to possibly change with the skip. I'm quite overwhelmed at the moment but I'm hoping to make all the changes people have suggested by some time next week.</p>
<p>The idea of adding names would definitely help the reader empathize with the victims - even if it's only mentioning the family's name, and maybe the first name of the kidnapped child.</p>
<p>As for signs of a struggle, this is something I could mention briefly - it certainly makes sense that the parents would try resisting, although I view the entity as anomalously strong and pretty much impossible to injure by mundane means, so their efforts would invariably be in vain. It might be a fun detail to add that a shotgun belonging to the father had been found at the scene, with both barrels discharged but no sign that the entity was even injured by this.</p>

